{"step":"3-blockscan-p3","measured":"bulk IN bytes after writing one byte value at one address of a register space the byte scans had not covered, on top of the baseline","harness":{"crates_rtl_head":"387a74c","harness_uncommitted":true},"unix_time":1791428436,"bench":"RTL2832U + R820T-family tuner, 28.8 MHz crystal, behind a USB analyzer with switchable TARGET-A power; no signal source, antenna input sees noise only","k":"header","block":"p3","candidate_space":"demodulator page 3 (request block 0, wIndex page 3), wValue = offset << 8 | 0x20 (step 1C): offset 0x00..=0xFF (wValue 0x0000..=0x00FF) x value 0x00..=0xFF, except the value the address holds when its candidate comes up (logged as kind s); iterated offset, value in ascending order with no reordering; 65536 candidates","bound":"Table 27 (p. 36) gives the demodulator pages 0-4; page 3 is where the documents place the readbacks (if_agc_val, rf_agc_val, aagc_lock, dagc_val, inc_det_cnt, sfreq_off, cfreq_off, mode_gi_idx: Tables 2, 9-12, all read-only). Offsets 0x00-0xFF, the whole page, as for pages 0-2","byte_addressing":"USB and system registers are 32-bit little-endian words (step 1A, data/step1-sys-usb-encoding.json; step 1D, data/step1-writes.json); byte reads inside them work (step 1A); each candidate is one byte written with wLength 1 at one address, and whether the chip takes a one-byte write into a 32-bit register is what the read-back (in / rb) records; demodulator pages are byte registers","already_known":"bit scan (data/step3-scan.jsonl, 2048 candidates on page 3): 0 bytes, 0 wedges, 0 disturbed baselines, 0 write or read errors; 60 offsets did not read back their restore (live values): 0x05-0x11, 0x14-0x1A, 0x1D, 0x1E, 0x20, 0x21, 0x24-0x27, 0x2A-0x2D, 0x2F, 0x30, 0x32, 0x34, 0x35, 0x37, 0x3A, 0x3B, 0x40, 0x41, 0x50-0x52, 0x5D, 0x5E, 0x60, 0x61, 0x66-0x6D, 0x72, 0x77, 0x79; 58 offsets read non-zero at the baseline. A value that does not read back is still measured","hazards":"none documented; page 3's documented registers are read-only","method":"plain, as data/step3-bytescan.jsonl: the value is written into the running chip with no restart between candidates (METHODS.md section 5: every declared space covered once before any is repeated with a variant)","settings_held_fixed":"documented-only baseline at 2400000 Hz; 4 x 16384 byte bulk transfers queued; window 50 ms right after the read-back, then a 200 ms follow-up window if any byte arrived, then a 50 ms window after the restore","window_justification":"the plain byte scan's (data/step3-bytescan.jsonl header): 4.8 MB/s fills a 16 KiB transfer every 3.4 ms, so 50 ms expects ~14.6 transfers (one-transfer quantisation 6.8 % < 20 % tolerance); any byte triggers the 200 ms follow-up, so a stream that starts up to ~50 ms after the write is still judged","streams_criterion":"within 20% of 2 x 2400000 bytes/s in the window or the follow-up","line_legend":"k: c candidate / s skip (the address's current value) / setup / recovery; o offset in the block (decimal); v value; orig the byte read before the write (null = the read failed); in the read-back after the write equals v; rb the read-back when it differs (absent when in); d bytes completed between candidates, discarded before the write (absent when 0); b bytes from the write to the end of the last window (window + follow-up); bps the follow-up window's bytes/s (absent without bytes); s streams; q the bulk detector's self-check from the previous candidate's last window to the end of the window, qf the same for the follow-up, qa for the after-restore window: [transfers submitted, completed, completed with an error, halts (Stall completions, each cleared by ClearFeature ENDPOINT_HALT), fewest transfers in flight, endpoint halted at any point 0/1]; e errors and events (absent when none); w wedged -> power cycle and re-baseline (next line k=recovery)","procedure":"read the byte (skip if equal); discard completed transfers; write the value; read it back; window; on bytes the follow-up; restore the original and verify by read-back; on bytes the after-restore window; chip answering?; baseline re-checked (DEMOD_CTL, AD_EN, en_bbin, rsamp_ratio, USB_SYSCTL DMA, USB_EPA_CFG, USB_EPA_CTL, USB_EPA_MAXPKT): reapplied if disturbed, power cycle if it does not hold; a chip that stops answering or keeps streaming after the restore is power-cycled and re-baselined; the scan does not stop on a hit"}
